#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:201
msgid "Your load order as a tree. Open a plugin to see what it changes, and a record to compare it across every plugin that defines it. Records are read and judged as you open them. Read-only: nothing here writes."
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:213
msgid "Plugin / type / record"
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:215
msgid "#"
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:256
msgid "Double-click a field for its full value across every plugin."
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:259
msgid "Colour says what this plugin is doing to the records beneath it:\n  blue = it defines them first\n  green = it changes them and nothing later disagrees\n  amber = it changes them, others disagreed, and it still wins\n  RED = it changes them and something later overrides the change\n  grey = it redefines them without changing anything\n\nRecords are read as you expand them, so colour fills in a moment after a group opens. A plugin takes the worst of whatever has been judged beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:292
msgid "Highlight only conflicts that lose work"
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/pluginview.py:299
msgid "Click a plugin to highlight the plugins it conflicts with, in purple.\n\nChecked (lost): only records where an edit is actually discarded -- the conflicts worth acting on. Needs a plugin summary, which opening this view starts on its own.\n\nUnchecked (broad): any record two plugins both touch, whether or not anything is lost."
msgstr ""

